  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/wild-betta-rutilans-green",
      "html": "<ul><li>From the Betta coccina complex.</li><li>IUCN Red List: Critically Endangered (an extremely high risk of extinction in the wild).</li><li>Sold as wild-caught Betta rutilans Green.</li><li>Max size: 1.2-1.5 inches.</li><li>TDS: 60-100.</li><li>pH: 5.0-6.5.</li><li>Temperature: 75-82°F.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/wild-betta-rutilans-green",
      "html": "<p>This species is identical in body and color to the red rutilans. However, some have a small hint of green on their body and fins. Apparently, some of these will have no green but we suspect they might have the genes.</p><p>Be sure to have the habitat ready before purchase.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/wild-betta-rutilans-green",
      "html": "<p>Carnivorous. They are currently fed live blackworms, frozen bloodworms and pellets.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/wild-betta-rutilans-green",
      "html": "<p>Moderately aggressive; males can be territorial when establishing breeding grounds. However, because of their small size, you can keep multiple pairs as long as you have enough space. Recommended 1 pair per 5 gallons.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/wild-betta-rutilans-green",
      "html": "<p>Bubblenester.</p>"
    }
  ],
